H("urlshortener-hld", "Design a URL shortener (TinyURL / bit.ly)", "Basic",
  ["Google", "Amazon", "Microsoft", "Uber", "Flipkart"],
  "ID generation, encoding, read-heavy caching, redirects, analytics.",
  ["Given a long URL, return a short unique URL (e.g. `sho.rt/aZ3kP9q`)", "Redirect short → long URL", "Optional: custom alias, expiry, click analytics"],
  ["Very low redirect latency (< 50 ms)", "Highly available (redirects must never fail)", "Short codes must be unique and not guessable in sequence", "Read-heavy: ~100 reads per write"],
  """- 100M new URLs/month → ~40 writes/s (peak ~100/s).
- Reads 100:1 → ~4,000 redirects/s (peak ~10k/s).
- 5 years: 100M × 60 = 6B URLs × ~500 bytes ≈ **3 TB**.
- Code length: base62 (a–z, A–Z, 0–9). 62⁷ ≈ 3.5 trillion → **7 characters** is plenty.""",
  """`POST /api/v1/urls {longUrl, customAlias?, expiresAt?}` → `201 {shortUrl}`
`GET /{code}` → `302 Location: <longUrl>` (or 301)
`GET /api/v1/urls/{code}/stats` → clicks by day/country""",
  """`urls(code PK, long_url, user_id, created_at, expires_at)` in a key–value store (DynamoDB/Cassandra) or sharded SQL; lookups are by `code` only.
`clicks` events → Kafka → analytics store (ClickHouse).""",
  {"rows": [["u:Users"], ["Load balancer"], ["Write API", "Redirect service"], ["ID generator (ranges)", "c:Redis cache"], ["db:URL store (KV)", "q:Click events (Kafka)"]],
   "edges": [["Users", "Load balancer"], ["Load balancer", "Write API", "POST"], ["Load balancer", "Redirect service", "GET /code"], ["Write API", "ID generator (ranges)", "next id"], ["Write API", "URL store (KV)"], ["Redirect service", "Redis cache", "hit 90%+"], ["Redirect service", "URL store (KV)", "miss"], ["Redirect service", "Click events (Kafka)"]]},
  ["Write: get a unique numeric ID from a range allocator (each server grabs 1,000 IDs at a time from ZooKeeper/DB), convert to base62, store `code → longUrl`.",
   "Read: look up code in Redis; on miss read the KV store and populate cache; return 302 redirect; publish a click event asynchronously.",
   "Custom alias: insert with a conditional write (fail if exists)."],
  ["**Generating codes**: (a) hash (MD5/SHA) of URL, take 7 chars, handle collisions by re-hashing with a salt; (b) counter + base62 (unique, no collisions, but sequential → shuffle bits or use a range per server); (c) pre-generated random key pool (Key Generation Service) marking used keys.",
   "**301 vs 302**: 301 is cached by browsers (less load, but you lose analytics); 302 keeps every click visible.",
   "**Cache**: 20% of URLs get 80% of traffic; LRU Redis cluster; CDN edge redirect for the hottest codes.",
   "**Expiry**: lazy delete on read + background cleanup job.",
   "**Abuse**: rate-limit creation, malware URL scanning, unguessable codes for private links."],
  ["KV store over SQL: single-key access, easy horizontal scaling.", "Async analytics so redirects stay fast."],
  ["How would you support 10x traffic?", "How to prevent two users getting the same custom alias?", "How to make codes unpredictable?"]),

