H("kvstore-hld", "Design a distributed key–value store (like DynamoDB / Cassandra)", "Advanced",
  ["Amazon", "Google", "Microsoft", "Apple"],
  "Partitioning, replication, consistency tuning, failure handling — the Dynamo paper.",
  ["`put(key, value)`, `get(key)`", "Values up to ~1 MB", "Tunable consistency"],
  ["Petabyte scale, horizontally scalable", "Highly available (always writable)", "Low latency (single-digit ms)", "Automatic failure detection and recovery"],
  "- 1M ops/s, 100 TB data, replication factor 3 → 300 TB raw across ~300 nodes of 1 TB.",
  "`PUT /kv/{key}` (body = value, header `consistency: QUORUM`) · `GET /kv/{key}`",
  "Per node: LSM-tree storage engine (commit log + memtable + SSTables + Bloom filters).",
  {"rows": [["u:Client"], ["Coordinator node"], ["db:Replica N1", "db:Replica N2", "db:Replica N3"]],
   "edges": [["Client", "Coordinator node", "put k"], ["Coordinator node", "Replica N1", "write"], ["Coordinator node", "Replica N2", "write"], ["Coordinator node", "Replica N3", "write"]]},
  ["Any node can coordinate; it hashes the key onto the **consistent-hash ring** (with virtual nodes) and finds the N replicas clockwise.",
   "Writes go to all N; success after **W** acks. Reads ask **R** replicas; return the newest version and **read-repair** stale ones.",
   "Each node writes to its commit log, then memtable; flushes SSTables; compacts in the background."],
  ["**Partitioning**: consistent hashing + vnodes; rebalancing moves only neighbour ranges.",
   "**Replication & consistency**: N=3, choose R/W (QUORUM for strong-ish, ONE for speed).",
   "**Versioning/conflicts**: vector clocks (Dynamo) or LWW timestamps (Cassandra).",
   "**Temporary failure**: sloppy quorum + hinted handoff.",
   "**Permanent failure / divergence**: anti-entropy with Merkle trees.",
   "**Membership & failure detection**: gossip protocol, phi-accrual detector.",
   "**Storage engine**: LSM tree for fast writes; Bloom filters for reads."],
  ["AP by default (always writable), at the cost of possible conflicts."],
  ["How do you add a node with zero downtime?", "How to support range scans?"]),

