H("dropbox-hld", "Design Google Drive / Dropbox (file storage and sync)", "Intermediate",
  ["Google", "Microsoft", "Amazon", "Dropbox"],
  "Chunking, dedup, metadata consistency, sync notifications, conflicts.",
  ["Upload/download files from any device", "Automatic sync across devices", "Share files/folders", "Version history"],
  ["Durable (never lose files)", "Efficient bandwidth (only changed parts)", "Strongly consistent metadata"],
  """- 50M DAU, 10 file changes/day → 500M changes/day ≈ 6k/s.
- 1B users × 10 GB quota... actual used ~2 GB avg → exabyte-scale storage with dedup.""",
  """`POST /files/upload-session` · `PUT /blocks/{hash}` (only missing blocks) · `POST /files/commit {path, blockHashes[], baseVersion}` · `GET /changes?cursor=` (long poll)""",
  """Metadata (SQL, sharded by user/namespace): `files(id, namespace, path, version, block_list, updated_at)`, `blocks(hash, size, storage_key, refcount)`, journal of changes per namespace.""",
  {"rows": [["u:Desktop client", "u:Phone client"], ["Metadata service", "Block service", "Notification service"], ["db:Metadata DB (SQL)", "db:Block storage (S3)"]],
   "edges": [["Desktop client", "Block service", "upload new blocks"], ["Desktop client", "Metadata service", "commit file version"], ["Block service", "Block storage (S3)"], ["Metadata service", "Metadata DB (SQL)"], ["Metadata service", "Notification service", "changed"], ["Notification service", "Phone client", "long poll"], ["Phone client", "Block service", "download missing blocks"]]},
  ["Client splits file into 4 MB blocks (content-defined), hashes them, asks which hashes are missing, uploads only those, then commits the new block list with the base version (optimistic concurrency).",
   "Other devices long-poll for changes, fetch new metadata and only the missing blocks."],
  ["Dedup by hash across all users.", "Conflicts: base-version mismatch → create 'conflicted copy'.", "Sharing: ACLs on namespaces; ReBAC model.", "Versioning: keep old block lists; garbage-collect unreferenced blocks.", "Encryption at rest per block; resumable uploads."]),

