H("uber-hld", "Design Uber / Ola (ride hailing)", "Advanced",
  ["Uber", "Google", "Amazon", "Microsoft", "Ola"],
  "Real-time location ingestion, geo matching, dispatch, trip state machine, payments.",
  ["Riders request rides; nearby drivers receive offers", "Live driver location on map, ETA", "Trip lifecycle, fare, payment, ratings"],
  ["Match in seconds", "Location updates every ~4 s from millions of drivers", "Highly available; no double-assignment of a driver"],
  """- 5M active drivers × 1 update / 4 s ≈ **1.25M location writes/s** — the key scaling challenge.
- 20M rides/day ≈ 230 ride requests/s (peaks much higher).""",
  """Driver: `POST /drivers/location {lat,lng}` (or WebSocket stream) · Rider: `POST /rides {pickup, drop}` → rideId · `GET /rides/{id}` · WebSocket for live updates · `POST /rides/{id}/accept` (driver).""",
  """Live locations: in-memory geo index (Redis GEO / H3 cells → driver IDs) with TTL, **not** a disk DB per update. Trips: SQL (state machine, strongly consistent). Location history: Kafka → data lake.""",
  {"rows": [["u:Rider app", "u:Driver app"], ["API gateway / WebSocket"], ["Ride service (state machine)", "Location service", "Matching/dispatch"], ["db:Trips DB", "c:Geo index (Redis, H3 cells)", "q:Kafka (location stream)"], ["Pricing / ETA (maps)", "Payments"]],
   "edges": [["Rider app", "API gateway / WebSocket"], ["Driver app", "API gateway / WebSocket", "location every 4s"], ["API gateway / WebSocket", "Location service"], ["Location service", "Geo index (Redis, H3 cells)"], ["Location service", "Kafka (location stream)"], ["API gateway / WebSocket", "Ride service (state machine)"], ["Ride service (state machine)", "Matching/dispatch"], ["Matching/dispatch", "Geo index (Redis, H3 cells)", "nearby drivers"], ["Ride service (state machine)", "Trips DB"], ["Ride service (state machine)", "Pricing / ETA (maps)"], ["Ride service (state machine)", "Payments"]]},
  ["Drivers stream locations → location service updates the geo index (cell → drivers) and Kafka.",
   "Rider requests → ride created (REQUESTED) → matching finds nearby available drivers ranked by ETA → offers sent one at a time (or batched) with timeout.",
   "Driver accepts → conditional update `driver.status AVAILABLE → ON_TRIP` prevents double assignment → trip ACCEPTED → live tracking via WebSocket → COMPLETED → fare + payment."],
  ["Geo index sharded by region/city (H3 cells).", "Matching consistency: atomic driver state transitions or a per-city dispatcher partition.", "Surge pricing from supply/demand per cell (stream processing).", "ETA from a routing engine (graph shortest paths with traffic).", "Payment via idempotent async flow after trip.", "Region-level isolation: a city's dispatch survives other failures."]),

